<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Chhatarpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1785 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Chhatarpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bundelkhand state ruled by a Ponwar family, whose lands included the temples of Khajuraho.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Chhatarpur town was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Maharaja Chhatrasal</a>, but around 1785 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soni-shah">Soni Shah</a>, a Ponwar who had served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundelas</a>, seized it from Chhatrasal's descendants and established his own state. The British confirmed the family's possession by sanad in 1806.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Chhatarpur was an 11-gun salute state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand-agency">Bundelkhand Agency</a> ruled by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a>. Its territory included the Chandela temples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a>. Maharaja Vishwanath Singh is portrayed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/j-r-ackerley">J. R. Ackerley's</a> memoir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindoo-holiday">Hindoo Holiday</a>, written after Ackerley served as his secretary in the 1920s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After independence Chhatarpur was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a> in 1948 and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956; it is now Chhatarpur district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chhatarpur-state.jpg" alt="Chhatarpur State" width="320" height="203"><figcaption>Image: Washiucho · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Chhatarpur.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1785 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chhatarpur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Soni Shah, Vishwanath Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chhatarpur</dd></dl></aside></div>
